

:: story.paintingWhatIs (old)
{=

(metadata:
"title", "That Thing in the Corner",
)

($funcMainContent:[{<!--?mainReading-->

It appears to be a ($funcReveal: "curtained window.", "curtain")|curtain)[ Or perhaps a shower.]

|curtain)[
<br>
A metal rack is installed about ten feet up the wall. Hanging from it is a makeshift curtain made up of translucent paper - you want to say glassine, but it is butcher's paper - veiling ($funcReveal: "whatever that is inside", "what") from ($funcReveal: "the world", "notReady"), and more importantly, preventing ($funcReveal: "you", "you") from staring at it all day long.
]

|what)[
<br>
($funcReveal: "//What// is behind the curtain?", "painting")
]

<!--trigger for ?yesBut-->
(set: _triggerYesBut to ($funcChainTrigger: "paintingQuestions", 3, "yesBut"))

|painting)[
<br>
Art.
]

|painting)[
<br>
($funcReveal: "A portrait?", "portrait")
]

|portrait)[
<br>
Sure, there was a girl - //Katherine// - who was the spark, but the kindling was already there.
<br>
If you lift the veil, you will see no face. Not hers. Perhaps not anyone's, though there will be eyes, and a nose, and a mouth, ($funcReveal: "and teeth", "teeth1")|teeth1)[($funcReveal: " and teeth", "teeth2")]|teeth2)[($funcReveal: " and teeth", "teeth3")]|teeth3)[($funcReveal: " and teeth", "teeth4")]|teeth4)[($funcReveal: " and teeth", "teeth5")]|teeth5)[($funcReveal: " and teeth..", "teeth6")]. 

|teeth6)[
<br>
No, this is too heavenly to be called a face._triggerYesBut
]
]<!--end ?portrait-->

|painting)[
<br>
($funcReveal: "A landscape?", "landscape")
]

|landscape)[
<br>
In every landscape, there is a ($funcReveal: "Sun", "suns")|suns)[` `- red upon the misty horizon, a perfect white dot upon a black sky, or gray hints within roiling clouds]. And yet, there is no ($funcReveal: "//land//", "dirt") on Earth that would see a light such as this!

|dirt)[
<br>
What need is there for dirt? You long to be above it all. This is //the thing itself//._triggerYesBut
]

]<!--end ?landscape-->


|painting)[
<br>
($funcReveal: "A still life?", "stillLife")
]

|stillLife)[
<br>

<!--trigger for ?noneOfThoseThings-->
(set: _triggerStillLife to ($funcChainTrigger: "stillLife", 2, "noneOfThoseThings"))

($funcReveal: "Still", "still")|still)[, but not dead, only sleeping._triggerStillLife]` `($funcReveal: "Life", "life")|life)[, but not bound toward old age or death._triggerStillLife]

|noneOfThoseThings)[
<br>
But, alas, this is none of those things. It is  ($funcReveal: "only a painting,", "onlyPainting")]

|onlyPainting)[` `a mimesis of something brought back from the slumbering heavens, a pale reminder for all that lives that there is yet a greater kind of life._triggerYesBut]

]<!--end ?stillLife-->


|yesBut)[
<br>
Yes, but what //is// it? ($funcReveal: "What will one sees if one looks?", "theSun")
]

|theSun)[
<br>
The Sun. It is a painting of ($funcReveal: "the Sun.", "mainDone")
]

|notReady)[
<br>
The world is not ready.
]

|you)[
<br>
Your Work is not yet done. It is calling out to you.
]


}],
[{<!--?mainDone-->

<!--just in case those 2 haven't shown-->
(t8n: "dissolve")(show: ?notReady)
(t8n: "dissolve")(show: ?you)

<!--link-->
($funcOutLink: "Lift the veil.", "And attempt to paint.", "story.painting1", [{
    <!--lock-->
    ($funcLock: (passage:)'s name)
}])

}],
false)